⍝ A⌹B stress test

⍝@ test3.

      )CLEAR
CLEAR WS

      ID←{ (⍳⍺) ∘.= (⍳⍵)}   ⍝ the ⍺×⍵ identity matrix (1 on diagonal)
      UT←{ (⍳⍺) ∘.> (⍳⍵)}   ⍝ upper triangle mask (1 below diagonal)

      TOL←0.001          ⍝ result tolerance

∇TEST COUNT;A;B;Z;M;N;REAL;∆;T;Ti
 ⍝
 ⍝ B:  a random M×N matrix,
 ⍝ Q:  an orthogonal M×M matrix,
 ⍝ R:  an upper triangle M×N matrix (same shape as B),
 ⍝ Ri: an upper triangle N×N matrix (the inverse of R), and
 ⍝
 ⍝ B ←→ Q ∘ R
 C1←COUNT
LOOP:
 N←1 + 8 ∣ ⎕RVAL 0                  ⍝ random number of columns (1..8)
 M←N + 4 ∣ 8⌈ ⎕RVAL 0               ⍝ random number of rows (≥ columns)
 MM←M M ◊ MN←M N ◊ NN←N N
 REAL← 1 ⍝ 2 | ⎕RVAL 0              ⍝ random type (real or complex)
 REAL← 0 0, REAL, ~REAL
 B←100 ∣ ⎕RVAL 2 (M, N) REAL        ⍝ random matrix B
 A←100 ∣ ⎕RVAL 1 (M)    REAL        ⍝ random result A for A = B∘X

 ⍝ test A⌹B
 ⍝
 Z←A ⌹ B
 →(M>N)/B_is_overspecified
 ∆←+/,∆×∆←A - ,B∘Z                  ⍝ ⌹ error
 →(TOL <∣ ∆)/∆_ERROR
B_is_overspecified:

 ⍝ test ⌹[X]B
 ⍝
 (Q R Ri)←⌹[⎕CT]Bin←B
 →(MN ≢ ⍴B) /RHO_B_ERROR
 →(MM ≢ ⍴Q) /RHO_Q_ERROR
 →(NN ≢ ⍴R) /RHO_R_ERROR
 →(NN ≢ ⍴Ri)/RHO_Ri_ERROR
 
 ⍝ Q is orthogonal/Hermitian
 ⍝
 →(0∈TOL > ∣(M ID M) - (⍉Q) ∘ Q)/ORTHO_Q_ERROR

 ⍝ R and Ri are upper triangular
 ⍝
 →(0∈TOL > ∣R  × NN↑(M UT N))  /UPPER_R_ERROR    ⍝ R is upper triangular
 →(0∈TOL > ∣Ri × (N UT N))     /UPPER_Ri_ERROR   ⍝ Ri is upper triangular
 →(0∈TOL > ∣(N ID N) - R ∘ Ri) /INV_R_ERROR      ⍝ Ri is R⁻¹
 →(0∈TOL > ∣∆←B - Q ∘ R)       /∆_ERROR2         ⍝ B is Q ∘ R

 →(0<COUNT←COUNT-1)⍴LOOP
 'OK' ◊ →0

RHO_B_ERROR:   '⍴B ERROR'        ◊  '⍴B:' (⍴B)                     ◊  →OUT
RHO_Q_ERROR:   '⍴Q ERROR'        ◊  '⍴B:' (⍴B)  ◊ '⍴Q:' (⍴Q)       ◊  →OUT
RHO_R_ERROR:   '⍴R ERROR'        ◊  '⍴B:' (⍴B)  ◊ '⍴R:' (⍴R)       ◊  →OUT
RHO_Ri_ERROR:  '⍴Ri ERROR'       ◊  '⍴B:' (⍴B)  ◊ '⍴Ri:' (⍴Ri)     ◊  →OUT
INV_R_ERROR:   'INV_R_ERROR: '   ◊  'B:' (2⍕B)
                                 ◊  'R:' (2⍕R)  ◊ 'Ri:' (2⍕Ri)     ◊  →OUT
UPPER_R_ERROR: 'UPPER R_ERROR'   ◊  2⍕R                            ◊  →OUT
UPPER_Ri_ERROR:'UPPER Ri_ERROR'  ◊  2⍕Ri                           ◊  →OUT
ORTHO_Q_ERROR: 'ORTHO_Q_ERROR:'  ◊  '⍴B:' (⍴B) ◊ ',B:' (,B)
                                    'Q:' (2⍕Q)  ◊ 'QQ:' (2⍕(⍉Q)∘Q) ◊  →OUT
∆_ERROR:       '∆_ERROR'
 'A:' (2⍕A) ◊ '⍴A' (⍴A)
 'B:' (2⍕B) ◊ '⍴B' (⍴B)
 'Z:' (2⍕Z) ◊ '⍴Z' (⍴Z)
 '∆:' ∆
 TOL <∣ ∆                                                          ◊  →OUT

∆_ERROR2:      '∆_ERROR2'
 'B:' (2⍕B)     ◊ '⍴B' (⍴B)
 'Q:' (2⍕Q)     ◊ '⍴Q' (⍴Q)
 'R:' (2⍕R)     ◊ '⍴R' (⍴R)
 'Q∘R:' (2⍕Q∘R) ◊ '⍴Q∘R' (⍴Q∘R)

OUT: "ERROR in pass" (C1 - COUNT) "of" C1
∇
      TEST 500
OK

      )CHECK
OK      - no stale functions
OK      - no stale values
OK      - no stale indices
OK      - no duplicate parents

      )CLEAR
CLEAR WS

      ⍝ Regression (Blake McBride, Bugs22 #2): ⌹0 discarded
      ⍝ bif_reciprocal()'s ErrorCode and returned 0 instead of
      ⍝ DOMAIN ERROR for a singular (zero) scalar argument.
      ⍝
      ⌹0
DOMAIN ERROR
      ⌹0
      ^
      )SIC

      ⌹0.0
DOMAIN ERROR
      ⌹0
      ^
      )SIC

      ⌹4
0.25
